Section: Flying with a radio
  The T1-S VTOL flies with a radio. A RadioMaster TX15 (or another EdgeTX radio) in USB
  joystick mode gives the sim the sticks and the switches. The sim sends them to ArduPilot
  as the radio signals of a real receiver, so the plane reacts as it does with the real
  radio. [[ArduPilot]] reads the sticks, the arm switch (SE) and the mode buttons (1 to 6 on the
  front of the radio). In the hover modes, the middle of the throttle stick holds the
  height. Above the middle the plane climbs, and below the middle it goes down.

  The first time, you set the radio up once (see Setting up the radio), and the sim saves it.
  After that, plug the radio in and start the station.

Background:
  Given the console is connected to a VTOL on the ground
  And the TX15 is ready

Vocabulary:
  State: the aileron stick is left | centred | right
    Set: move the aileron stick {value}: all the way left, in the middle, or all the way right
    Shows: left: the first number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1250
    Shows: centred: the first number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1500
    Shows: right: the first number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1750
  State: the VTOL's wings are level | banked
    Shows: level: the horizon in the PFD is flat, and the roll reading is near 0
    Shows: banked: the horizon in the PFD is tilted, and the roll reading is more than 10° from 0
  State: the last landing is soft | hard
    Shows: soft: the plane touches the ground at less than 2 m/s, and the HUD of the sim does not say CRASHED
    Shows: hard: the plane touches the ground at 2 m/s or more

  Event: the pilot switches to forward flight
    Say: push the throttle stick all the way up, pull the elevator stick back a little, and press button 3 on the front of the radio. The wing motors tilt forward and the plane speeds up
  Event: the pilot switches back to a hover
    Say: centre the elevator stick, put the throttle stick in the middle, and press button 2 on the front of the radio. The plane slows down and the wing motors tilt up

  Event: the pilot switches to QHOVER
    Say: press button 1 on the front of the radio. The plane stays in the air, and the wind can move it
  Event: the pilot switches to cruise
    Say: press button 4 on the front of the radio, with the throttle stick up. The wing motors tilt forward and the plane flies on its wing
  Event: the pilot sends the plane home
    Say: press button 6 on the front of the radio. The plane flies to home, and lands there

  Phrase: the VTOL is hovering over the field
    Say: put the arm switch on, press button 2 and push the throttle stick up. Wait until the plane is 15 m above the field. Keep the throttle stick up
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    And the flight is hovering
    And the height above home is at least 15 m
    And the throttle stick is high

  Phrase: the VTOL is cruising in FBWA
    Say: lift off as above. Push the throttle stick all the way up, pull the elevator stick back a little, and press button 3. The wing motors tilt forward. Wait until the plane flies on its wing
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the autopilot mode is FBWA
    And the flight is cruising
    And the height above home is at least 15 m
    And the throttle stick is high
